;; FH-ROOT-006 — hydration adopts, and a divergence is reported.
;;
;; ADOPTION is proven by NODE IDENTITY, not by text. The server's markup is
;; put into the container, the exact DOM nodes it created are captured, and
;; after hydration those SAME node objects must still be mounted. A root
;; that quietly discarded the server render and client-rendered instead
;; would produce identical text and pass any assertion written about it.
;;
;; The mismatch half needs the same care in the other direction. React's
;; `onRecoverableError` is the only signal here, so a harness that never
;; receives it reports nothing and passes on broken and correct HTML alike.
;; The fixture therefore pins a KNOWN-BAD server body as well as the correct
;; one: the divergent case must produce the diagnostic, and the matching
;; case must produce none. Neither assertion means anything without the
;; other.
;;
;; What React recovers from is bounded, and the boundary is React's own: a
;; text mismatch or a missing / extra / wrong-type element reaches the
;; callback; an ATTRIBUTE-only divergence does not, because React documents
;; that it makes no guarantee to patch attribute mismatches. That row is
;; here so the boundary is pinned as a fact rather than discovered later as
;; a surprise.
{:fh/id "FH-ROOT-006"
 :fh/law
 "v/hydrate-root ADOPTS server-rendered markup — the server's own DOM nodes survive the mount — and a divergence React recovers from is REPORTED as :rf.ssr/hydration-mismatch carrying the root-id, composed over any host :on-recoverable-error and bounded to the adoption window, while identity opts supplied client-side are refused with :rf.error/root-manifest-invalid."

 :view  :greeting
 :props {:name "world"}
 :root-id :re-frame.freehand.root-views/greeting

 ;; The server's bytes for `[greeting {:name "world"}]`.
 :server-html "<section id=\"greeting\"><h1 id=\"title\">Hello</h1><p id=\"who\">world</p></section>"

 ;; The matching case: the server's nodes are still the mounted nodes, and
 ;; nothing was reported.
 :match {:adopted true
         :same-nodes ["#greeting" "#title" "#who"]
         :mismatches 0}

 ;; The KNOWN-BAD case — the harness's own proof that it can see anything at
 ;; all. The text under #who disagrees, which is squarely inside what React
 ;; recovers from.
 :divergent-html "<section id=\"greeting\"><h1 id=\"title\">Hello</h1><p id=\"who\">SOMEBODY ELSE</p></section>"
 :divergent {:mismatches-at-least 1
             :operation :rf.ssr/hydration-mismatch
             :where     re-frame.freehand/hydrate-root
             :recovery  :warned-and-replaced
             ;; React's recovery is a REPLACEMENT: the page ends up carrying
             ;; the client's truth, never the server's stale value under a
             ;; tree that disagrees with it.
             :final-text "world"}

 ;; A host callback is composed OVER, never clobbered: the framework emits
 ;; first, then the host's own callback runs.
 :host-callback {:invocations-at-least 1}

 ;; Identity comes from the server. Supplying it client-side is a conflict,
 ;; not an override.
 :identity-opts-refused
 [{:opts {:root-id :fh.root/other}          :error :rf.error/root-manifest-invalid}
  {:opts {:identifier-prefix "mine-"}       :error :rf.error/root-manifest-invalid}
  {:opts {:disambiguator :left}             :error :rf.error/root-manifest-invalid}]}
